This Kotlin Multiplatform library combines specification implementations with
ports of permissively licensed compression code.

The DEFLATE inflate path is an altered Kotlin translation of Mark Adler's puff
(2002-2013), via KiteTorrent and libtorrent. puff carries a zlib-style license,
not a public-domain dedication; its original notice is retained in Inflate.kt.
The DEFLATE encoder originated in KitePDF's FlateDecode encoder and its
canonical Huffman assignment follows zlib's trees.c (Jean-loup Gailly and
Mark Adler). Deflate.kt retains the zlib copyright and license notice. The
length-limited builder independently implements binary package-merge; Zopfli's
Apache-2.0 katajainen.c was consulted as an algorithm and validation reference.

Format references consulted for porting (study only, not redistributed; see
reference/REFERENCES.md) are each under permissive licenses: zlib (zlib), XZ for Java
(0BSD / public domain), Apache Commons Compress (Apache-2.0), lz4 (BSD-2), zstd
(BSD-3), brotli (MIT), snappy (BSD-3).

RAR archives are read from RARLAB's published format description (technote), not
from UnRAR source, whose license forbids using it to build a RAR-compatible
compressor; ArchiveKodec will never create RAR archives. ACE / StuffIt are excluded:
no clean open reference exists for them.

Some test fixtures are third-party data, used unmodified: RAR test
archives from libarchive's test suite (BSD-2-Clause, Copyright (c) 2003-2018 Tim
Kientzle and the libarchive contributors).
